usage: ht-role [-h]
               {self,neighbors,inputs,dependents,execution,evidence,assignment,brief,approve,commitment,status,delivery,environment,describe}
               ...

positional arguments:
  {self,neighbors,inputs,dependents,execution,evidence,assignment,brief,approve,commitment,status,delivery,environment,describe}
    execution           your activation as of this turn's start (what your
                        position owes, what changed since your last turn) and,
                        live, what you owe that changed since the turn started
    evidence            build evidence references or paper provenance
                        deterministically
    assignment          show the world's work assignment, your package first
    brief               show the world's brief of what the objective asks: its
                        owner, the commit it was read at and its full text
    approve             review owner: approve the current delivery for
                        release; the system binds every position's current
                        revision, verifies the delivery and records the
                        approval, or says why it cannot
    commitment          show your recorded commitment, or record it in your
                        own words with --file
    status              show the system-computed state of the whole world:
                        owners, requirements and their providers, assignment,
                        brief, assembly errors, review, release, activity, and
                        every commitment
    delivery            list or write the delivery assembled from current
                        revisions
    environment         install or reuse dependencies in the private workspace

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
